## Two Laws (non-negotiable)

### Law 1 — Understand dimensions BEFORE any change

Before **add · remove · refactor · rule · schema · posting · UI flow**:

```
① SCOPE      — files · DOMAIN_MAP module · wave boundary
② LINKS      — callers · callees · DI · events · shared DTOs (grep)
③ SHARED     — schema SQLite+PG · BranchId · RBAC · posting chain
④ IMPACT     — accounting · security · workflow · RTL UX · tests
⑤ CONFLICTS  — OPEN_ITEMS · parallel wave · removed behavior · CEEF scope
⑥ VERIFY PLAN— which build/test/gate proves safety?
```

**Mandatory Plan Mode** when: 5+ modules · migration/schema · posting/Golden/ZATCA · API/behavior removal · new always-on rule.

**Skip only for:** typo · single obvious test-red fix · user question-only (Inquiry).

### Law 2 — Write memory AFTER verified change

After **verify PASS** (or explicit ⏭ external boundary):

Append one entry to `docs/PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml`:

| Field | Required |
|-------|----------|
| `id` | `MEM-NNN` sequential |
| `date` | ISO date |
| `type` | `fix` · `feature` · `removal` · `rule` · `decision` · `lesson` · `note` |
| `problem` | what was wrong or needed (1–2 sentences) |
| `affected` | modules · tests · workflows impacted |
| `how` | what we did (1–2 sentences) |
| `verify` | command or evidence path |
| `links` | `ceef` · `rule` · `files` · `detail` (optional) |

**Tiering:**

| Size | Where |
|------|-------|
| Small fix · single rule | `PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml` only |
| 3+ modules · architectural fork | `docs/memory/MEM-NNN-slug.md` + YAML row |
| Full wave close | CEEF in `تقارير/` + YAML row pointing to CEEF |

**Never:** claim "done" without verify · write MEM before verify · CEEF for every typo.

